Pi4 uses or adapts the following upstream implementations and architectures:

The bundled viewer is a reduced migration of the project's point_cloud_viewer:
quaternion trackball controls, page layout/styles, point shaders and sorting,
screen-space picking, binary-array decoding, motion geometry scopes, progressive
frame display, current-frame highlights, and seeded dynamic-track selection.
It runs independently and does not import that project at runtime.

DINOv3: facebookresearch/dinov3; image encoder and axial rotary encoding.
License text: licenses/DINOV3.txt.

MoGe: microsoft/MoGe; point decoding and sparse depth-refinement architecture.
License text: licenses/MOGE.txt.

CoWTracker: facebookresearch/cowtracker; RGB features, dense iterative warping,
cross-view refinement, and confidence/visibility outputs.
License text: licenses/COWTRACKER.txt.

SAM 2: facebookresearch/sam2; Hiera-small and feature-pyramid image encoding.
License text: licenses/SAM2.txt.

Depth Anything V2: DepthAnything/Depth-Anything-V2; DPT feature-fusion blocks.
License text: licenses/DEPTH_ANYTHING_V2.txt.

PyTorch Image Models: huggingface/pytorch-image-models; tracking ViT architecture.
Apache-2.0 text: licenses/APACHE-2.0.txt.

Pi3: yyfz/Pi3; geometry-decoder and camera-readout architecture.
License text: licenses/PI3.txt.

FlexGEMM: JeffreyXiang/FlexGEMM; separately installed sparse-convolution backend.
Its own distribution retains its license and notices.

Three.js: mrdoob/three.js; bundled browser rendering and TrackballControls.
License text: licenses/THREE.txt. Only these runtime files are retained from
the larger point-cloud viewer; no server-rendering or recording code is used.
